  "helpTitle": "How to survive",
  "helpGoalTitle": "Goal",
  "helpGoalBody": "Each zombie carries a plate with four digits. Keep the digits in order and add operators and one \"=\" to build a true equation. Example: 8 1 3 1 → √(8 + 1) = 3**1.",
  "helpBuildTitle": "Loading the plate",
  "helpBuildBody": "Tap a gap between the digits to aim (the glowing cursor), then tap the operators on the ammo belt. Tap an operator on the plate to remove it. Digits can never be joined: 1 2 is not twelve. Precedence: × and ÷ come before + and −; √ and ∛ apply only to the number right after them and ! only to what comes before it (√9! = (√9)! = 6). Use parentheses to change it. The ! of a non-integer uses its integer part: (√8)! = 2! = 2.",
  "helpKeyboardTitle": "Keyboard (typing of the dead!)",
  "helpKeyboardBody": "Type + - * / ( ) ! = directly. ** or ^ is a power, s is √, c is ∛, | is the absolute value, [ ] is floor and '{ }' is ceiling. Typing the next digit just moves past it. ← → move the cursor, Backspace removes, Enter fires and Esc clears.",
  "helpLevelsTitle": "Levels",
  "helpLevelsBody": "Easy has every operator and is the only level that accepts non-integer divisions such as 5/2. Intermediate drops floor and ceiling, Advanced also drops powers and the cube root, and Hard only keeps + - × ÷, parentheses and the absolute value.",
  "helpScoreTitle": "Score",
  "helpScoreBody": "Harder levels are worth more points. Answering fast and keeping a streak gives bonuses. A hint costs 75% of the plate’s points. You can skip a plate at any time, but the zombie keeps coming from where it was, and a plate you solved never appears again at that level.",
  "close": "Close",

